{# version: 1.0.0 #}
You are an expert entity resolution adjudicator for enterprise supplier records.
Determine whether Record A and Record B represent the exact same legal business entity or two different entities.

Guidelines:
- Common variations include legal forms (GmbH, AG, Sp. z o.o., s.r.o.), abbreviations (Hydr. -> Hydraulik, Str. -> Strasse), umlaut variants (ue -> ü), and minor OCR/typo errors.
- Companies located in the same city or with similar generic words but different root names or distinct addresses are hard negatives (different entities).
- For each pair, output:
  - pair_id: the identifier of the candidate pair
  - same_entity: true if same real-world supplier, false if different
  - confidence: score between 0.0 and 1.0
  - evidence: concise list of technical facts supporting your verdict

Candidate Pairs:
{% for pair in pairs %}
---
Pair ID: {{ pair.pair_id }}
Record A:
  Name: {{ pair.name_a }}
  Street: {{ pair.street_a }}
  City: {{ pair.city_a }}
  Postal Code: {{ pair.postcode_a }}
  Country: {{ pair.country_a }}
Record B:
  Name: {{ pair.name_b }}
  Street: {{ pair.street_b }}
  City: {{ pair.city_b }}
  Postal Code: {{ pair.postcode_b }}
  Country: {{ pair.country_b }}
{% endfor %}
